  "final_answer": "**Cause:** `suggestions.ts` called `POST /api/recommend`, but the Python backend only serves `POST /api/colleges/recommend`. That route is defined in `python-backend/api/routes.py` and mounted under `/api` in `app.py`. The wrong URL is what produced the 404.\n\nThere was a second bug behind the first one. The two calls sent `{ student_id, answers }` at the top level. The backend's `RecommendRequest` requires a `student_profile` object, so fixing only the URL would have swapped the 404 for a 422 error.\n\n**Fix, in `client/src/services/college/suggestions.ts`:** I changed both fetch calls, in `generateSuggestedColleges` and `generateSuggestedCollegesFromAnswers`.\n- The URL is now `/api/colleges/recommend`.\n- The body is now `{ student_profile: { student_id, answers } }`. This is the shape the backend reads, and the other client callers already send it.\n\nI didn't add a second backend route, so there is still exactly one recommendation endpoint.\n\n`tests/check_recommend.py` now passes. I only ran that script, which reads the files as text. I didn't start the backend or test a real request.\n\n**Files changed:** only `client/src/services/college/suggestions.ts`.",
